From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: win32u: Trace status-bar text DCs without application strings.

AI-assisted (Codex), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not
submitted upstream.

Diagnostic only, 2026-11-07. No Windows behaviour is asserted or changed.
The maintainer's public-API snapshots show overlapping pixels through the
status-bar DC after GPU ray tracing in a maximised Inventor window; window
geometry and the observer's DC origin remain unchanged. Restore Down
cleans the text and maximising again restores the fault. Screen-DC
snapshots were black, so they do not distinguish composition.

With +sbdiag, identify status-bar DCs by their public class name and record
numeric state at the actual ExtTextOut entry, opaque backend fill, glyph
backend call and return. Include clipping shapes and DIB surface mapping.
Do not print text, glyphs, titles, pixel data or file paths. Keep this out
of patches/series; it diagnoses the fault and is not a proposed fix.

